    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid, this is not possible to the extent you describe.\r\n\r\n'mini.notify' module is meant to show on-demand and LSP notifications. Overriding built-in notifications is out of scope of 'mini.notify', as this is still not an easy to implement and maintain functionality.\r\n\r\nThat said, you can mimic this behavior by creating an autocommand which gets triggered on every buffer write:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('BufWritePost', {\r\n  callback = function(args)\r\n    local path = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf)\r\n    if path ~= '' then path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(path, ':~:.') end\r\n    -- Assumes `vim.notify()` overridden by 'mini.notify'\r\n    vim.notify('Saved ' .. vim.inspect(path))\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid, this is not possible to the extent you describe.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">'mini.notify' module is meant to show on-demand and LSP notifications. Overriding built-in notifications is out of scope of 'mini.notify', as this is still not an easy to implement and maintain functionality.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">That said, you can mimic this behavior by creating an autocommand which gets triggered on every buffer write:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('BufWritePost', {\n  callback = function(args)\n    local path = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf)\n    if path ~= '' then path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(path, ':~:.') end\n    -- Assumes `vim.notify()` overridden by 'mini.notify'\n    vim.notify('Saved ' .. vim.inspect(path))\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>BufWritePost<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_buf_get_name</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">~=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">fnamemodify</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>:~:.<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Assumes `vim.notify()` overridden by 'mini.notify'</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">notify</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Saved <span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">inspect</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span>))\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "I am afraid, this is not possible to the extent you describe.\n'mini.notify' module is meant to show on-demand and LSP notifications. Overriding built-in notifications is out of scope of 'mini.notify', as this is still not an easy to implement and maintain functionality.\nThat said, you can mimic this behavior by creating an autocommand which gets triggered on every buffer write:\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('BufWritePost', {\n  callback = function(args)\n    local path = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf)\n    if path ~= '' then path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(path, ':~:.') end\n    -- Assumes `vim.notify()` overridden by 'mini.notify'\n    vim.notify('Saved ' .. vim.inspect(path))\n  end,\n})",
