                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "I implemented the following solution to make it work:\r\n\r\nAs you suggested,\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufWritePost\", {\r\n  callback = function(args)\r\n    local path = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf)\r\n    if path ~= \"\" then\r\n      path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(path, \":~:.\")\r\n    end\r\n    vim.notify = MiniNotify.make_notify()\r\n    vim.notify(\"Saved \" .. vim.inspect(path))\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\n***I set `cmdheight` to `0`***\r\n\r\n`vim.opt.cmdheight = 0`\r\n\r\nSince cmdheight is set to 0, it doesn't show any info while recording a macro. Therefore, the following autocmd was handy for me:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nfunction M.autocmds()\r\n  local autocmd = vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd\r\n\r\n  autocmd(\"RecordingEnter\", {\r\n    callback = function()\r\n      vim.opt.cmdheight = 1\r\n    end,\r\n  })\r\n\r\n  autocmd(\"RecordingLeave\", {\r\n    callback = function()\r\n      vim.opt.cmdheight = 0\r\n    end,\r\n  })\r\nend\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I implemented the following solution to make it work:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As you suggested,</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(&quot;BufWritePost&quot;, {\n  callback = function(args)\n    local path = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf)\n    if path ~= &quot;&quot; then\n      path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(path, &quot;:~:.&quot;)\n    end\n    vim.notify = MiniNotify.make_notify()\n    vim.notify(&quot;Saved &quot; .. vim.inspect(path))\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>BufWritePost<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_buf_get_name</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">~=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">fnamemodify</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>:~:.<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">notify</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniNotify</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">make_notify</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">notify</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Saved <span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">inspect</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span>))\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em><strong>I set <code class=\"notranslate\">cmdheight</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">0</code></strong></em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">vim.opt.cmdheight = 0</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Since cmdheight is set to 0, it doesn't show any info while recording a macro. Therefore, the following autocmd was handy for me:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"function M.autocmds()\n  local autocmd = vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd\n\n  autocmd(&quot;RecordingEnter&quot;, {\n    callback = function()\n      vim.opt.cmdheight = 1\n    end,\n  })\n\n  autocmd(&quot;RecordingLeave&quot;, {\n    callback = function()\n      vim.opt.cmdheight = 0\n    end,\n  })\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">M</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">autocmds</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">autocmd</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>RecordingEnter<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">cmdheight</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n  })\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>RecordingLeave<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opt</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">cmdheight</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n  })\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "I implemented the following solution to make it work:\nAs you suggested,\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufWritePost\", {\n  callback = function(args)\n    local path = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf)\n    if path ~= \"\" then\n      path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(path, \":~:.\")\n    end\n    vim.notify = MiniNotify.make_notify()\n    vim.notify(\"Saved \" .. vim.inspect(path))\n  end,\n})\nI set cmdheight to 0\nvim.opt.cmdheight = 0\nSince cmdheight is set to 0, it doesn't show any info while recording a macro. Therefore, the following autocmd was handy for me:\nfunction M.autocmds()\n  local autocmd = vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd\n\n  autocmd(\"RecordingEnter\", {\n    callback = function()\n      vim.opt.cmdheight = 1\n    end,\n  })\n\n  autocmd(\"RecordingLeave\", {\n    callback = function()\n      vim.opt.cmdheight = 0\n    end,\n  })\nend",
